---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../utils/paths';

const sampleClusterYaml = `apiVersion: krabka.io/v1alpha1
kind: Kafka
metadata:
  name: demo
  namespace: default
spec:
  kafkaVersion: "4.0.0"
  listeners:
    - name: plain
      port: 9092
      type: internal
      tls: false
    - name: tls
      port: 9094
      type: internal
      tls: true
  interBrokerListenerName: plain
  authorization:
    type: simple
    superUsers: ["ANONYMOUS"]
---
apiVersion: krabka.io/v1alpha1
kind: KafkaNodePool
metadata:
  name: brokers
  namespace: default
  labels:
    krabka.io/cluster: demo
spec:
  roles: [Controller, Broker]
  replicas: 3
  nodeIdStart: 0
  storage:
    type: PersistentClaim
    size: 50Gi
    deleteClaim: true`;

const installOperatorYaml = `# Add Helm chart repository and install the operator
helm repo add krabka https://krabka.io/charts
helm repo update
helm install krabka-operator krabka/krabka-operator --version 0.4.1 \\
  --namespace krabka-system --create-namespace`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Kubernetes Operator (krabka-operator)"
  description="Kubernetes operator reconciling Kafka clusters, node pools, topics, users, and rebalances via krabka.io/v1alpha1 CRDs."
  currentSlug="/docs/operator"
>
  <div class="space-y-6 font-sans">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <div class="text-xs text-gray-400 mb-1">
        Kubernetes · Developer Preview
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">Kubernetes Operator</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-sm max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        Declarative cluster reconciliation, node pool orchestration, rolling upgrades, and automated partition rebalancing via <code class="text-krab-300 font-mono text-xs">krabka-operator</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-xs text-amber-300 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-amber-200">Developer Preview Notice:</strong>
        <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">krabka-operator</code> is under active development. Core Kafka cluster reconciliation, custom resource definitions, and Helm deployment charts are published.
      </div>

      <p>
        The Krabka Operator reconciles standard Kubernetes Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs) into running StatefulSets, headless Services, ConfigMaps, TLS Secrets, and broker configurations. Cluster topology is decoupled across <code class="font-mono text-xs text-krab-300">Kafka</code> (cluster-wide version, listeners, CA) and <code class="font-mono text-xs text-krab-300">KafkaNodePool</code> (roles, replicas, storage claims).
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Sample Kafka & NodePool Manifest</h2>
      <p>
        A minimal <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">krabka.io/v1alpha1</code> configuration declaring a three-broker combined Controller/Broker quorum with persistent volume storage:
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span>Kafka & KafkaNodePool CRDs:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-colors text-xs" data-copy={sampleClusterYaml}>
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <CodeBlock code={sampleClusterYaml} lang="yaml" />
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs)</h2>
      <p>
        All custom resource definitions managed by the operator in API group <code class="text-krab-300 font-mono">krabka.io/v1alpha1</code>:
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
          <thead class="bg-slate-950/80 border-b border-white/10 uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 font-semibold font-sans">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Kind</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Declared Responsibility</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 font-sans">
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5"><td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono font-medium text-krab-300">Kafka</td><td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-gray-400">A cluster: version label, listeners, cluster and clients CA, authorization, metrics, tiered storage</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5"><td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono font-medium text-krab-300">KafkaNodePool</td><td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-gray-400">A pool of nodes with its own roles (Controller, Broker), replicas, image, resources, and storage</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5"><td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono font-medium text-krab-300">KafkaTopic</td><td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-gray-400">A topic, its partition count, replication factor, and configuration</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5"><td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono font-medium text-krab-300">KafkaUser</td><td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-gray-400">A principal, its authentication (SCRAM-SHA-256/512, TLS, externally managed TLS, delegation token), ACLs, and quotas</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5"><td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono font-medium text-krab-300">KafkaConnector</td><td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-gray-400">A PostgreSQL CDC source connector (postgresSource)</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5"><td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono font-medium text-krab-300">KafkaRebalance</td><td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-gray-400">A partition rebalance request (full, addBrokers or removeBrokers), served by the krabka-rebalancer</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5"><td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono font-medium text-krab-300">SchemaRegistry</td><td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-gray-400">A Confluent-compatible schema registry deployment</td></tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5"><td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono font-medium text-krab-300">KafkaGrpcGateway</td><td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-gray-400">A gRPC gateway deployment</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-xs text-amber-300 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-amber-200">Component images:</strong>
        With no <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">spec.image</code>, a <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">KafkaConnector</code> runs <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">ghcr.io/krabka-io/krabka-connect-worker:v0.4.0</code> and a <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">KafkaGrpcGateway</code> runs <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">ghcr.io/krabka-io/krabka-gateway:v0.4.0</code>. Both tags are published on ghcr.io. Set <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">spec.image</code> on the resource, or <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">connectorImage</code> and <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">gatewayImage</code> in the chart values, to use another tag, a digest, or a mirror. The <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">SchemaRegistry</code> default, <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">krabka-schema-registry:0.4.0</code>, is published.
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Scope & Architectural Boundaries</h2>
      <p>
        <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-operator</code> is scoped strictly to Kafka broker and cluster components. The Postgres-compatible compute substrate (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">gres</code>) is managed separately from the CRDs listed above.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Installing via Helm</h2>
      <p>
        Deploy the operator using the official Helm chart. The chart installs the CRDs from its own <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">crds/</code> directory on first install; Helm does not update them on upgrade, so apply them again from the chart you upgrade to (see the chart's install notes). The <a href={getPath('/docs/quickstart')} class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300">quickstart</a> runs the same install end to end with pinned images:
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span>Helm Installation:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-colors text-xs" data-copy={installOperatorYaml}>
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <CodeBlock code={installOperatorYaml} lang="bash" />
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Related Resources</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose pt-1">
        <a href={getPath('/docs/helm-charts')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Helm Chart Repository →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">GPG signing key, chart index, and verification instructions for Krabka charts.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={getPath('/features/operator')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Operator Feature Tour →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Overview of rolling upgrades, CRD reconciliation, and automated partition rebalancing.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
